     "text": "{\"related_campaigns\": [], \"kill_chain_stage\": \"initial access / execution\", \"prior_alert_context\": \"This appears to be an opportunistic exploitation attempt against a web API endpoint. If successful, follow-up alerts would typically include: (1) successful command execution logs showing shell activity under web service context, (2) outbound network connections to malware.sh host indicating payload download, (3) file creation/execution of downloaded binaries, (4) privilege escalation attempts if the attacker tries to break out of web process context. The targeting of /etc/passwd and use of wget suggests the attacker is probing for Linux systems and intends to establish persistence or lateral movement capability. Prior context may include vulnerability scanning, authentication brute-force, or other web reconnaissance against the API service.\", \"threat_severity_hint\": \"high\"}",
