   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\":[{\"id\":\"T1059\",\"name\":\"Command and Scripting Interpreter\",\"tactics\":[\"Execution\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The alert detects an attempt to execute arbitrary shell commands (cat /etc/passwd; wget malware.sh) through command injection in a web application parameter.\"},{\"id\":\"T1105\",\"name\":\"Ingress Tool Transfer\",\"tactics\":[\"Command and Control\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The injected command includes a wget malware.sh attempt, which is a direct example of downloading and transferring malicious tools to a compromised system.\"},{\"id\":\"T1212\",\"name\":\"Exploitation for Credential Access\",\"tactics\":[\"Credential Access\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The command injection attack targets the /etc/passwd file, indicating an attempt to extract sensitive system credentials or authentication data through vulnerability exploitation.\"}],\"identity_signals\":null,\"key_findings\":\"An external attacker attempted a multi-stage command injection attack against an admin endpoint, combining credential extraction (/etc/passwd enumeration) with malware download capabilities (wget). The WAF successfully denied the malicious request at the perimeter before any execution occurred on internal systems.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"severity_rationale\":\"This is a blocked attack from an external source (192.0.2.201) targeting a perimeter web service. The WAF's signature-based detection prevented execution, with no evidence that the attack reached internal hosts or accounts. While the payload is sophisticated and demonstrates intent to establish command execution and tool transfer, the control functioned as designed and no internal compromise is indicated.\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"recommended_response\":\"Confirm WAF rule effectiveness and log retention; review admin endpoint access controls and consider network segmentation restrictions on that path. Correlate source IP 192.0.2.201 against threat intelligence feeds and consider blocking at network perimeter if associated with known threat actors. Verify that the targeted /admin/execute endpoint has proper input validation and authentication in place. Monitor for similar injection attempts or escalation patterns from this or related source IPs over the next 24\u201348 hours.\",\"rounds_used\":0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "diagnostics": null,
