     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.75, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.80, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"The investigation demonstrates solid foundational analysis with well-reasoned severity assessment and practical response steps. The ATT&CK mapping is mostly sound, though T1212 (Exploitation for Credential Access) is somewhat tangential since /etc/passwd enumeration is better characterized as reconnaissance or credential dumping rather than exploitation for access\u2014consider refining technique selection. The analysis could be strengthened by explicitly documenting the absence of internal indicators (no lateral movement, no authentication logs triggered) and by clarifying whether the WAF logged the full payload for future correlation. Overall, this is a competent triage that appropriately de-escalates a blocked attack while maintaining appropriate monitoring posture.\"}",
